hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18940","Waki narrated to us, Misar and al-Masudi narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Sari, from Amr ibn Hurayth, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, reciting in the Fajr prayer: When the sun is folded up, and I heard him saying: And the night when it departs."
"18941","Waki narrated to us, Musawir al-Warraq narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Amr ibn Hurayth, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed the people wearing a black turban."
"18942","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from one who heard Amr ibn Hurayth saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed in his sandals."
"18943","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Suddi, one who heard Amr ibn Hurayth narrated to me, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying in patched sandals."
"18944","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj al-Muharibi, from Abu al-Aswad, from Amr ibn Hurayth, he said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and heard him reciting: I swear by the retreating, moving, hiding stars."
"18945","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Sari, from Amr ibn Hurayth, he said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recite in the Fajr prayer: And the night when it departs."
